Z||000000||FieroJET||10-11-2001||11:21 PM||||Does anyone know what to replace the slave cylinder "push rod" (the rod between the slave and clutch fork arm) with?  It was brought to my attention by a mech that one end of my rod was worn flat causing the rod to not push squarely on the slave cyl plunger causing premature failure of the seal & plunger. Also is this legit or BS? I've been through 3 slaves in a year.<BR>Thanks for any info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowCG||10-12-2001||12:26 AM||||I've used an old Chevy pushrod;they're hollow and the hardened,ball-shaped ends can be pressed back into the rod after you've shortened it to the proper length.<BR>That sounds like it could be true indeed.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||10-12-2001||12:38 PM||||I would think you could grind it back round and slide the slave a little closer. I think the angle of the rod as it pushes is the problem ( providing the slave bore is A-1 ). I replaced my 84 clutch lever with an 85 that was a little longer. Had to change the angle of slave to stop seal from wear out.||||reg||1
